cond when we think about  accountability in minneapolis half of  police officers who are fired are  rehired  and that's because of the way the  contract is structured and these are  things that are  fixes that we need political leaders who  are courageous enough to deal with  in minneapolis today the police chief of  mayor could ban chokeholds today they  could do it  it would take no vote no nothing they  could do it they choose not to  and that's what we see all across the  country the lack of courageous  leadership  in office martin luther king the third  do we had a republican strategist peter  lumar john earlier who said what he was  seeing in minneapolis  is not civil disobedience and peaceful  protest which is protected under the  constitution and he was making the  argument that donald trump is reacting  to local authorities pointing out they  are mainly democrats not  acting fast enough so the federal  government has to step in and looking at  donald trump's twitter he's  probably making the same argument what  do you make of that that  it's not violent protest is not the same  as civil disobedience  look again i do not  uh i i cannot  condone violence but what i will say  is if you have your foot on someone's  neck as this literally happened  constantly and you're telling people  don't push my foot away off  your neck it seems a little preposterous  i mean obviously all of this is politics  whatever donald trump is doing he's  doing for his base  um and unfortunately he isn't in a very  powerful position  and there are those who support this and  look at what he says  as the rule of law and do not have the  sensitivity to understand  the people have been pushed their backs  have been pushed up against the wall  now again i may choose a different  method a methodology to address but i  understand  what people are going through and if you  look at this this is not just black folk  in fact in minnesota it's probably a  large  part of the crowd maybe even whit